==============================================================================
B1a. e_anti(n): Fable 2S(n-1)/(2^n*5n)  vs  Kimi [2(n-1)-B(n)]/(5n), n=2..30
==============================================================================
  bridge identity holds exactly for all n=2..30: True
  (algebra: min(u,v)=(u+v-|u-v|)/2 gives Fable e=(5n-E|8K-5n|)/(10n);
   E|Z|=2E[Z^+]-E[Z] with E[8K-5n]=-(n+4) gives Kimi form. Both verified.)

  n | e_anti exact      | s1=1/2-e  | t1=2/s1 (BP1 target) | 4/e (kill comp.)
   2 | 1/5              | 3/10      | 20/3                 | 20          
