==============================================================================
B2a. Rademacher max-identity E|Y+wR| = E max(|Y|,|w|): EC sanity (exact)
==============================================================================
  2000 random discrete Y, exact: identity holds = True
  Proof (DR): condition on Y=y: (|y+w|+|y-w|)/2 = max(|y|,|w|) since
  |y+w|+|y-w| = (|y|+|w|) + ||y|-|w|| = 2 max(|y|,|w|). QED.
  Monotonicity: g_n(S+{i}) = E max(g-r.v., w_i) >= g_n(S); equality iff
  |Y_S| >= w_i a.s. Hence argmax S=[n] (antipodal). Strictness per-coord EC'd below.

==============================================================================
B2b. Direct-enumeration audit of support reduction e({0,q}) = (5n-g_n(supp q))/(10n)
      and codebook counts (n<=8 brute force over prototypes p=0 fixed)
==============================================================================
  n=2: weighted-majority vs formula mismatches=0; Hamming-nearest strictly worse in 1 cases; #optimal q (p=0 fixed) = 2 (expect 1); total optimal codebooks = 4 = 2^(n-1)
  n=3: weighted-majority vs formula mismatches=0; Hamming-nearest strictly worse in 2 cases; #optimal q (p=0 fixed) = 1 (expect 1); total optimal codebooks = 4 = 2^(n-1)
  n=4: weighted-majority vs formula mismatches=0; Hamming-nearest strictly worse in 4 cases; #optimal q (p=0 fixed) = 1 (expect 1); total optimal codebooks = 8 = 2^(n-1)
  n=5: weighted-majority vs formula mismatches=0; Hamming-nearest strictly worse in 15 cases; #optimal q (p=0 fixed) = 1 (expect 1); total optimal codebooks = 16 = 2^(n-1)
  n=6: weighted-majority vs formula mismatches=0; Hamming-nearest strictly worse in 31 cases; #optimal q (p=0 fixed) = 1 (expect 1); total optimal codebooks = 32 = 2^(n-1)
  n=7: weighted-majority vs formula mismatches=0; Hamming-nearest strictly worse in 63 cases; #optimal q (p=0 fixed) = 1 (expect 1); total optimal codebooks = 64 = 2^(n-1)
  n=8: weighted-majority vs formula mismatches=0; Hamming-nearest strictly worse in 127 cases; #optimal q (p=0 fixed) = 8 (expect 8); total optimal codebooks = 1024 = n*2^(n-1)
  n=8 check: 8*2^7 = 1024
  FINDING: support functional e=(5n-g_n(S))/10n = error under WEIGHTED-majority
  (optimal) assignment; Hamming-nearest deterministic tie rules are strictly
  worse for supports containing the heavy coord with 1..n-2 lights (and at
  antipodal support for even n). Mod-8 tie law + codebook counts stand, with
  achievability by weighted-majority codes (n=8: enumerator 3440 attained).
